            <description><![CDATA[<!--
  The what's-new fragment Sparkle shows inside its update window for 1.0.

  A FRAGMENT AND NOT A PAGE: no DOCTYPE, no <html>, no <head>, no <body>.
  `generate_appcast --embed-release-notes` puts this text inside appcast.xml,
  where it ends up covered by the appcast's own EdDSA signature, and Sparkle
  renders it in a small web view inside the update window.

  HAND-WRITTEN, ONE FILE PER VERSION, until the docs suite exists (D182, D186).
  Callout renders its equivalent from `Tools/docs/notes/current.js` — the same
  source as its Release Notes PDF — so the two cannot drift (its D385). This app
  has no docs pipeline and no Release Notes to drift from, so the honest form is
  a file somebody writes and `publish-update.sh` refuses to publish without.
  When the docs question is answered, this becomes a generated file and that
  check becomes Callout's freshness comparison.

  ONE HONEST LINE. ~~This build has never been cut, signed or sent to
  anybody~~ — SUPERSEDED IN PLACE, Sep 6, 2026 (D188): `./release.sh` has now
  been run once, and its first run found two defects rather than producing a
  cut. Nothing has been sent to anybody and no `--publish` has happened, so the
  fragment below is unchanged: there is still nothing to claim beyond what the
  version is. `RELEASES.md` carries the status and the verifier flips its row
  after a successful cut.
-->
<h2>DFP EXtractoR 1.0</h2>
<p>
  Multilayer OpenEXR sequences to ProRes and PNG, with Cryptomatte matte
  extraction and light-group export — and, from this build on, the app can
  update itself.
</p>
